@startuml sequence-send-mail

!include sequence-styling.puml.inc

actor "Office Manager" as OfficeManager
participant "little-trotter-invoice" as WebApp
participant "kotlin-email" as MailApp
database "PostgreSQL\n<size:10>[Schema: mail]</size>" as DB
queue "NATS JetStream\n<size:10>[Stream: mail.send]</size>" as MailQueue
participant "SMTP Server\n<size:10>[Relay]</size>" as SMTP
database "RustFS\n<size:10>[Object Store]</size>" as S3 <<storage>>

OfficeManager -> WebApp: click "Rechnung per E-Mail senden"
WebApp -> MailApp: POST /mail/api/compose (draft)
MailApp --> WebApp: return drafted message

OfficeManager -> WebApp: confirm send
WebApp -> MailApp: POST /mail/api/send
MailApp -> DB: persist mail_journal (status=QUEUED, archiveStatus=PENDING)
MailApp -> MailQueue: publish mail.send.order
MailApp --> WebApp: queued accepted
WebApp --> OfficeManager: notification: queued

MailQueue -> MailApp: consume mail.send.order
MailApp -> SMTP: transmit MIME (.eml) via TLS
SMTP --> MailApp: 250 OK (queued)
MailApp -> DB: markTerminal(SENT)
MailApp -> S3: store sent .eml

opt Archive Copy configured
  MailApp -> SMTP: transmit journal copy to archive address
end

== Deterministic Archive Packaging ==

MailApp -> MailApp: buildAndStore(journalId)
MailApp -> S3: read .eml & authored JSON
MailApp -> MailApp: sign payloads (Ed25519)
MailApp -> MailApp: build deterministic <journalId>.tar.gz\n(original/, signed/, manifest.json)
MailApp -> S3: put archive.tar.gz
MailApp -> DB: markArchived(ARCHIVED, s3Key, sha256)

$SequenceStorageLegend()
@enduml
